**Q13: Explain multi-stage builds and their benefits.**

A:
Multi-stage builds use multiple FROM statements to reduce final image size.

```dockerfile
# Stage 1: Builder
FROM golang:1.19 AS builder
WORKDIR /app
COPY . .
RUN go build -o app main.go

# Stage 2: Runtime (only ~10MB)
FROM alpine:3.17
COPY --from=builder /app/app /
ENTRYPOINT ["/app"]

# Final image size: ~50MB (not 1GB with Go SDK)
```

Benefits:
- Removes build tools from final image
- Reduces security attack surface
- Faster deployment

